Hi,

I loaded an ecdsa P256 key, which was generated by openssl, into TPM. Once =
the key is not longer needed for my use case, I would like to unload the ke=
y. Can I know what tpm2 tool command that I can use to unload the external =
key?
I am assuming if I don't unload the key, the key context/memory will foreve=
r be held by TPM (unless reboot). If I never release that and I keep loadin=
g new keys into TPM, the TPM will eventually run out of memory.

ref: https://github.com/tpm2-software/tpm2-tools/blob/master/man/tpm2_loade=
xternal.1.md

openssl ecparam -genkey -name prime256v1 -noout -out ec256-key-pair.pem
tpm2_loadexternal -C n -G ecc -r ec256-key-pair.pem -c eckey.ctx

Thanks
